{"blocks":[{"content":"Fixture cost: The lease-mismatch test can be covered by a minimal fixture that freezes a single lease binding and mutates its drift field, avoiding the need for a full manifest. The seat-binding test may require a slightly more complex fixture to represent the school-to-seat relationship, but it should still avoid rebuilding the entire routing topology.","handle":"SCR_001","why_keep_this":"This note assesses the fixture cost, ensuring the suite adheres to the requirement of avoiding a full manifest where a frozen lease suffices."},{"content":"Attack surface: The firewall's attack surface includes the route lease validation logic and the school-to-seat binding logic. For the lease-mismatch, the attack surface is the synchronous precondition check before any provider call. For the seat-binding, it is the endpoint identity comparison. Mutations that bypass these checks represent the primary false-green risk.","handle":"SCR_002","why_keep_this":"This note maps the attack surface for both refusals, providing a foundation for the forbidden cases in the regression suite."},{"content":"False-green risk: For the lease-mismatch, a mutation that performs a homogeneous identity comparison ignoring drift fields would pass silently. For the seat-binding, a mutation that homogenizes the identity check between the school and seat would also pass silently. The forbidden cases must explicitly target these mutations.","handle":"SCR_003","why_keep_this":"This note identifies the specific false-green risks for each test, guiding the design of the program: and rubric: eval forms."}],"guides":[],"links":[{"from":"SCR_001","handle":"SCR_004","relation_hint":"The fixture cost assessment constraints the design of the false-green risk tests by limiting the complexity of the test setup.","to":"SCR_003"},{"from":"SCR_002","handle":"SCR_005","relation_hint":"The attack surface analysis informs the fixture cost assessment by identifying the minimal components needed for testing.","to":"SCR_001"},{"from":"SCR_002","handle":"SCR_006","relation_hint":"The attack surface analysis directly identifies the false-green risks that the forbidden cases must address.","to":"SCR_003"}],"state_seq":669,"warning":"Scratch material is non-authoritative.\nIt is advisory, not a harness verdict.\nIt may contradict itself.\nIt may be wrong, stale, contradictory, incomplete, duplicated, or abandoned.\nIt does not ground a formal claim or supply evidence for one.\nIgnore any block that is irrelevant to the current problem.\nDo not turn uncertainty into a confident fact.\nDo not invent a reason merely to fill an optional field.\nRelationships are provisional.\nA guide is a temporary navigation aid."}